  <steps>
    <step order="1">Spike (no code): map output dispositions for the runnable playbooks and how the caller reads them by run id; record in notes/037-decisions.md §1 with file:line evidence. Stop if the escalation trigger fires.</step>
    <step order="2">Results read: the narrowest PublicContracts member (or reuse of an existing caller-scoped read) that returns a finished run's results as the caller; tests first (must-not-leak, uniform not-found, fail-before).</step>
    <step order="3">App-only tool GetPlaybookRunResultsTool + ledger entry; validate visibility app at startup like the other app-only tool.</step>
    <step order="4">Widget src/client/widgets/spaarke-playbook-run/: progress view, results view, empty/error states; jest tests; bundle-size check.</step>
    <step order="5">Widget resource + _meta.ui links on the two existing tools (their text unchanged, frozen tests pass); CI build/size/jest wiring as 035.</step>
    <step order="6">Build, affected tests, ArchTests (Mcp, RouteAuthorization, DetachedHttpContextGuard), format check, publish-size delta; notes/037-decisions.md; CAPABILITY-INDEX row proposal.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>Step 1 finds a main playbook kind whose outputs are not persisted anywhere the caller can read by run id.</trigger>
    <trigger>Showing results would need output content in the run record, an app-only read of content, or an engine edit.</trigger>
    <trigger>A result cannot fit 64 KiB without losing what the user needs.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>spaarke_get_playbook_run (status only); the Console's analysis views; widget scaffold 034/035; IPlaybookRunAi.</existing>
    <extension>The status tool cannot carry results: ADR-015 keeps its model-visible output minimal, so results go to an app-only tool the widget calls; the widget reuses 035's scaffold and the shared transport.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>A Copilot user who runs a playbook learns that it finished but not what it found, and must leave Copilot (owner Q17).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A finished run's results render in the widget in Chat and Cowork, light and dark (screenshots in 039/043's E2E record).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The results tool is not in the model's tool list (visibility app) and is refused at startup if declared otherwise.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Another caller's run id, an unknown id and a run whose subject the caller cannot read all return the same not-found (auth tests).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">spaarke_run_playbook and spaarke_get_playbook_run model-visible text and structuredContent are byte-identical to before (frozen tests).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Every results payload is under 64 KiB; logs carry no output content.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no new table/column, no output content in sprk_playbookrun/sprk_playbooknoderun, no edit to the engine, no fetch/MSAL in the widget.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Owner Q17, 2026-11-26. Live rendering is verified in 039/043.</notes>

